It&#8217;s the second ultra-premium all-inclusive resort from the Rixos brand in Egypt (Picture: Rixos Premium Magawish Bay View)



No one tells you quite how exhausting a scuba diving holiday is.&nbsp;

I’d just stepped off an Egyptian ‘liveaboard’ in Hurghada — a week-long underwater safari that is arguably the best way to explore the Red Sea.&nbsp;

Surrounded by some of the healthiest coral reefs in the world and some serious marine life, I’d spent my days diving with oceanic white-tip sharks and marvelling at dramatic seascapes, while battling strong currents.&nbsp;

Immersive diving holidays for are rapidly growing in popularity, with the market value expected to triple by 2034 as more people are pulled toward adventure travel.

This is contributing to a tourism boom around the Red Sea, a place where the waters are warm, excursions are relatively affordable, and wild dolphins play among spectacular shipwrecks and reef ecosystems.&nbsp;

It is, indeed, magical. But honestly, I needed a holiday from my holiday after that one; four scuba dives a day for a week is not for the faint-hearted.

This is where Rixos Premium Magawish Bay View comes in.

Driving up to the expansive resort on a private road, past horse stables where rabbits hop in the greenery, you can feel your worries float away as you enter the region&#8217;s newest five-star all-inclusive.

Still gently rocking even on shore, the Rixos was exactly what I needed.&nbsp;

